59455	2	1063	12	Some of you are saying, “I am a follower of Paul.” Others are saying, “I follow Apollos,” or “I follow Peter,” or “I follow only Christ.”
59456	2	1063	13	Has Christ been divided into factions? Was I, Paul, crucified for you? Were any of you baptized in the name of Paul? Of course not!
59457	2	1063	14	I thank God that I did not baptize any of you except Crispus and Gaius,
59458	2	1063	15	for now no one can say they were baptized in my name.
59459	2	1063	16	(Oh yes, I also baptized the household of Stephanas, but I don’t remember baptizing anyone else.)
59460	2	1063	17	For Christ didn’t send me to baptize, but to preach the Good News—and not with clever speech, for fear that the cross of Christ would lose its power.
59461	2	1063	18	The message of the cross is foolish to those who are headed for destruction! But we who are being saved know it is the very power of God.
59462	2	1063	19	As the Scriptures say,\n“I will destroy the wisdom of the wise\n    and discard the intelligence of the intelligent.”
59463	2	1063	20	So where does this leave the philosophers, the scholars, and the world’s brilliant debaters? God has made the wisdom of this world look foolish.
59464	2	1063	21	Since God in his wisdom saw to it that the world would never know him through human wisdom, he has used our foolish preaching to save those who believe.
59465	2	1063	22	It is foolish to the Jews, who ask for signs from heaven. And it is foolish to the Greeks, who seek human wisdom.
59466	2	1063	23	So when we preach that Christ was crucified, the Jews are offended and the Gentiles say it’s all nonsense.
59467	2	1063	24	But to those called by God to salvation, both Jews and Gentiles, Christ is the power of God and the wisdom of God.
59514	2	1066	1	So look at Apollos and me as mere servants of Christ who have been put in charge of explaining God’s mysteries.
59468	2	1063	25	This foolish plan of God is wiser than the wisest of human plans, and God’s weakness is stronger than the greatest of human strength.
59469	2	1063	26	Remember, dear brothers and sisters, that few of you were wise in the world’s eyes or powerful or wealthy when God called you.
