60853	2	1124	10	She must be well respected by everyone because of the good she has done. Has she brought up her children well? Has she been kind to strangers and served other believers humbly? Has she helped those who are in trouble? Has she always been ready to do good?
60854	2	1124	11	The younger widows should not be on the list, because their physical desires will overpower their devotion to Christ and they will want to remarry.
60855	2	1124	12	Then they would be guilty of breaking their previous pledge.
60856	2	1124	13	And if they are on the list, they will learn to be lazy and will spend their time gossiping from house to house, meddling in other people’s business and talking about things they shouldn’t.
60857	2	1124	14	So I advise these younger widows to marry again, have children, and take care of their own homes. Then the enemy will not be able to say anything against them.
60858	2	1124	15	For I am afraid that some of them have already gone astray and now follow Satan.
60859	2	1124	16	If a woman who is a believer has relatives who are widows, she must take care of them and not put the responsibility on the church. Then the church can care for the widows who are truly alone.
60860	2	1124	17	Elders who do their work well should be respected and paid well, especially those who work hard at both preaching and teaching.
60861	2	1124	18	For the Scripture says, “You must not muzzle an ox to keep it from eating as it treads out the grain.” And in another place, “Those who work deserve their pay!”
60862	2	1124	19	Do not listen to an accusation against an elder unless it is confirmed by two or three witnesses.
60863	2	1124	20	Those who sin should be reprimanded in front of the whole church; this will serve as a strong warning to others.
60864	2	1124	21	I solemnly command you in the presence of God and Christ Jesus and the highest angels to obey these instructions without taking sides or showing favoritism to anyone.
60865	2	1124	22	Never be in a hurry about appointing a church leader. Do not share in the sins of others. Keep yourself pure.
60866	2	1124	23	Don’t drink only water. You ought to drink a little wine for the sake of your stomach because you are sick so often.
60867	2	1124	24	Remember, the sins of some people are obvious, leading them to certain judgment. But there are others whose sins will not be revealed until later.
60868	2	1124	25	In the same way, the good deeds of some people are obvious. And the good deeds done in secret will someday come to light.
60869	2	1125	1	All slaves should show full respect for their masters so they will not bring shame on the name of God and his teaching.
60870	2	1125	2	If the masters are believers, that is no excuse for being disrespectful. Those slaves should work all the harder because their efforts are helping other believers who are well loved.\nTeach these things, Timothy, and encourage everyone to obey them.
60871	2	1125	3	Some people may contradict our teaching, but these are the wholesome teachings of the Lord Jesus Christ. These teachings promote a godly life.
60872	2	1125	4	Anyone who teaches something different is arrogant and lacks understanding. Such a person has an unhealthy desire to quibble over the meaning of words. This stirs up arguments ending in jealousy, division, slander, and evil suspicions.
60873	2	1125	5	These people always cause trouble. Their minds are corrupt, and they have turned their backs on the truth. To them, a show of godliness is just a way to become wealthy.
60874	2	1125	6	Yet true godliness with contentment is itself great wealth.
60875	2	1125	7	After all, we brought nothing with us when we came into the world, and we can’t take anything with us when we leave it.
60876	2	1125	8	So if we have enough food and clothing, let us be content.
60877	2	1125	9	But people who long to be rich fall into temptation and are trapped by many foolish and harmful desires that plunge them into ruin and destruction.
60878	2	1125	10	For the love of money is the root of all kinds of evil. And some people, craving money, have wandered from the true faith and pierced themselves with many sorrows.
60879	2	1125	11	But you, Timothy, are a man of God; so run from all these evil things. Pursue righteousness and a godly life, along with faith, love, perseverance, and gentleness.
60880	2	1125	12	Fight the good fight for the true faith. Hold tightly to the eternal life to which God has called you, which you have declared so well before many witnesses.
60881	2	1125	13	And I charge you before God, who gives life to all, and before Christ Jesus, who gave a good testimony before Pontius Pilate,
60882	2	1125	14	that you obey this command without wavering. Then no one can find fault with you from now until our Lord Jesus Christ comes again.
60883	2	1125	15	For,\nAt just the right time Christ will be revealed from heaven by the blessed and only almighty God, the King of all kings and Lord of all lords.
60884	2	1125	16	He alone can never die, and he lives in light so brilliant that no human can approach him. No human eye has ever seen him, nor ever will. All honor and power to him forever! Amen.
60885	2	1125	17	Teach those who are rich in this world not to be proud and not to trust in their money, which is so unreliable. Their trust should be in God, who richly gives us all we need for our enjoyment.
60886	2	1125	18	Tell them to use their money to do good. They should be rich in good works and generous to those in need, always being ready to share with others.
60887	2	1125	19	By doing this they will be storing up their treasure as a good foundation for the future so that they may experience true life.
60888	2	1125	20	Timothy, guard what God has entrusted to you. Avoid godless, foolish discussions with those who oppose you with their so-called knowledge.
60889	2	1125	21	Some people have wandered from the faith by following such foolishness.\nMay God’s grace be with you all.
60890	2	1126	1	This letter is from Paul, chosen by the will of God to be an apostle of Christ Jesus. I have been sent out to tell others about the life he has promised through faith in Christ Jesus.
60891	2	1126	2	I am writing to Timothy, my dear son.\nMay God the Father and Christ Jesus our Lord give you grace, mercy, and peace.
60892	2	1126	3	Timothy, I thank God for you—the God I serve with a clear conscience, just as my ancestors did. Night and day I constantly remember you in my prayers.
60893	2	1126	4	I long to see you again, for I remember your tears as we parted. And I will be filled with joy when we are together again.
60894	2	1126	5	I remember your genuine faith, for you share the faith that first filled your grandmother Lois and your mother, Eunice. And I know that same faith continues strong in you.
60895	2	1126	6	This is why I remind you to fan into flames the spiritual gift God gave you when I laid my hands on you.
60896	2	1126	7	For God has not given us a spirit of fear and timidity, but of power, love, and self-discipline.
60897	2	1126	8	So never be ashamed to tell others about our Lord. And don’t be ashamed of me, either, even though I’m in prison for him. With the strength God gives you, be ready to suffer with me for the sake of the Good News.
60898	2	1126	9	For God saved us and called us to live a holy life. He did this, not because we deserved it, but because that was his plan from before the beginning of time—to show us his grace through Christ Jesus.
60899	2	1126	10	And now he has made all of this plain to us by the appearing of Christ Jesus, our Savior. He broke the power of death and illuminated the way to life and immortality through the Good News.
60900	2	1126	11	And God chose me to be a preacher, an apostle, and a teacher of this Good News.
60901	2	1126	12	That is why I am suffering here in prison. But I am not ashamed of it, for I know the one in whom I trust, and I am sure that he is able to guard what I have entrusted to him until the day of his return.
60902	2	1126	13	Hold on to the pattern of wholesome teaching you learned from me—a pattern shaped by the faith and love that you have in Christ Jesus.
60903	2	1126	14	Through the power of the Holy Spirit who lives within us, carefully guard the precious truth that has been entrusted to you.
60904	2	1126	15	As you know, everyone from the province of Asia has deserted me—even Phygelus and Hermogenes.
60905	2	1126	16	May the Lord show special kindness to Onesiphorus and all his family because he often visited and encouraged me. He was never ashamed of me because I was in chains.
60906	2	1126	17	When he came to Rome, he searched everywhere until he found me.
60907	2	1126	18	May the Lord show him special kindness on the day of Christ’s return. And you know very well how helpful he was in Ephesus.
60908	2	1127	1	Timothy, my dear son, be strong through the grace that God gives you in Christ Jesus.
60909	2	1127	2	You have heard me teach things that have been confirmed by many reliable witnesses. Now teach these truths to other trustworthy people who will be able to pass them on to others.
60910	2	1127	3	Endure suffering along with me, as a good soldier of Christ Jesus.
60911	2	1127	4	Soldiers don’t get tied up in the affairs of civilian life, for then they cannot please the officer who enlisted them.
60912	2	1127	5	And athletes cannot win the prize unless they follow the rules.
60913	2	1127	6	And hardworking farmers should be the first to enjoy the fruit of their labor.
60914	2	1127	7	Think about what I am saying. The Lord will help you understand all these things.
60915	2	1127	8	Always remember that Jesus Christ, a descendant of King David, was raised from the dead. This is the Good News I preach.
60916	2	1127	9	And because I preach this Good News, I am suffering and have been chained like a criminal. But the word of God cannot be chained.
60917	2	1127	10	So I am willing to endure anything if it will bring salvation and eternal glory in Christ Jesus to those God has chosen.
60918	2	1127	11	This is a trustworthy saying:\nIf we die with him,\n    we will also live with him.
60919	2	1127	12	If we endure hardship,\n    we will reign with him.\nIf we deny him,\n    he will deny us.
60920	2	1127	13	If we are unfaithful,\n    he remains faithful,\n    for he cannot deny who he is.
60921	2	1127	14	Remind everyone about these things, and command them in God’s presence to stop fighting over words. Such arguments are useless, and they can ruin those who hear them.
60922	2	1127	15	Work hard so you can present yourself to God and receive his approval. Be a good worker, one who does not need to be ashamed and who correctly explains the word of truth.
60923	2	1127	16	Avoid worthless, foolish talk that only leads to more godless behavior.
60924	2	1127	17	This kind of talk spreads like cancer, as in the case of Hymenaeus and Philetus.
60925	2	1127	18	They have left the path of truth, claiming that the resurrection of the dead has already occurred; in this way, they have turned some people away from the faith.
60926	2	1127	19	But God’s truth stands firm like a foundation stone with this inscription: “The Lord knows those who are his,” and “All who belong to the Lord must turn away from evil.”
60927	2	1127	20	In a wealthy home some utensils are made of gold and silver, and some are made of wood and clay. The expensive utensils are used for special occasions, and the cheap ones are for everyday use.
60928	2	1127	21	If you keep yourself pure, you will be a special utensil for honorable use. Your life will be clean, and you will be ready for the Master to use you for every good work.
60929	2	1127	22	Run from anything that stimulates youthful lusts. Instead, pursue righteous living, faithfulness, love, and peace. Enjoy the companionship of those who call on the Lord with pure hearts.
60930	2	1127	23	Again I say, don’t get involved in foolish, ignorant arguments that only start fights.
60931	2	1127	24	A servant of the Lord must not quarrel but must be kind to everyone, be able to teach, and be patient with difficult people.
60932	2	1127	25	Gently instruct those who oppose the truth. Perhaps God will change those people’s hearts, and they will learn the truth.
60933	2	1127	26	Then they will come to their senses and escape from the devil’s trap. For they have been held captive by him to do whatever he wants.
60934	2	1128	1	You should know this, Timothy, that in the last days there will be very difficult times.
60935	2	1128	2	For people will love only themselves and their money. They will be boastful and proud, scoffing at God, disobedient to their parents, and ungrateful. They will consider nothing sacred.
60936	2	1128	3	They will be unloving and unforgiving; they will slander others and have no self-control. They will be cruel and hate what is good.
60937	2	1128	4	They will betray their friends, be reckless, be puffed up with pride, and love pleasure rather than God.
60938	2	1128	5	They will act religious, but they will reject the power that could make them godly. Stay away from people like that!
60939	2	1128	6	They are the kind who work their way into people’s homes and win the confidence of vulnerable women who are burdened with the guilt of sin and controlled by various desires.
60940	2	1128	7	(Such women are forever following new teachings, but they are never able to understand the truth.)
60941	2	1128	8	These teachers oppose the truth just as Jannes and Jambres opposed Moses. They have depraved minds and a counterfeit faith.
60942	2	1128	9	But they won’t get away with this for long. Someday everyone will recognize what fools they are, just as with Jannes and Jambres.
60943	2	1128	10	But you, Timothy, certainly know what I teach, and how I live, and what my purpose in life is. You know my faith, my patience, my love, and my endurance.
60944	2	1128	11	You know how much persecution and suffering I have endured. You know all about how I was persecuted in Antioch, Iconium, and Lystra—but the Lord rescued me from all of it.
60945	2	1128	12	Yes, and everyone who wants to live a godly life in Christ Jesus will suffer persecution.
60946	2	1128	13	But evil people and impostors will flourish. They will deceive others and will themselves be deceived.
60947	2	1128	14	But you must remain faithful to the things you have been taught. You know they are true, for you know you can trust those who taught you.
60948	2	1128	15	You have been taught the holy Scriptures from childhood, and they have given you the wisdom to receive the salvation that comes by trusting in Christ Jesus.
60949	2	1128	16	All Scripture is inspired by God and is useful to teach us what is true and to make us realize what is wrong in our lives. It corrects us when we are wrong and teaches us to do what is right.
60950	2	1128	17	God uses it to prepare and equip his people to do every good work.
60951	2	1129	1	I solemnly urge you in the presence of God and Christ Jesus, who will someday judge the living and the dead when he comes to set up his Kingdom:
60952	2	1129	2	Preach the word of God. Be prepared, whether the time is favorable or not. Patiently correct, rebuke, and encourage your people with good teaching.
60953	2	1129	3	For a time is coming when people will no longer listen to sound and wholesome teaching. They will follow their own desires and will look for teachers who will tell them whatever their itching ears want to hear.
60954	2	1129	4	They will reject the truth and chase after myths.
60955	2	1129	5	But you should keep a clear mind in every situation. Don’t be afraid of suffering for the Lord. Work at telling others the Good News, and fully carry out the ministry God has given you.
60956	2	1129	6	As for me, my life has already been poured out as an offering to God. The time of my death is near.
60957	2	1129	7	I have fought the good fight, I have finished the race, and I have remained faithful.
60958	2	1129	8	And now the prize awaits me—the crown of righteousness, which the Lord, the righteous Judge, will give me on the day of his return. And the prize is not just for me but for all who eagerly look forward to his appearing.
60959	2	1129	9	Timothy, please come as soon as you can.
60960	2	1129	10	Demas has deserted me because he loves the things of this life and has gone to Thessalonica. Crescens has gone to Galatia, and Titus has gone to Dalmatia.
60961	2	1129	11	Only Luke is with me. Bring Mark with you when you come, for he will be helpful to me in my ministry.
60962	2	1129	12	I sent Tychicus to Ephesus.
60963	2	1129	13	When you come, be sure to bring the coat I left with Carpus at Troas. Also bring my books, and especially my papers.
60964	2	1129	14	Alexander the coppersmith did me much harm, but the Lord will judge him for what he has done.
60965	2	1129	15	Be careful of him, for he fought against everything we said.
60966	2	1129	16	The first time I was brought before the judge, no one came with me. Everyone abandoned me. May it not be counted against them.
60967	2	1129	17	But the Lord stood with me and gave me strength so that I might preach the Good News in its entirety for all the Gentiles to hear. And he rescued me from certain death.
60968	2	1129	18	Yes, and the Lord will deliver me from every evil attack and will bring me safely into his heavenly Kingdom. All glory to God forever and ever! Amen.
60969	2	1129	19	Give my greetings to Priscilla and Aquila and those living in the household of Onesiphorus.
60970	2	1129	20	Erastus stayed at Corinth, and I left Trophimus sick at Miletus.
60971	2	1129	21	Do your best to get here before winter. Eubulus sends you greetings, and so do Pudens, Linus, Claudia, and all the brothers and sisters.
60972	2	1129	22	May the Lord be with your spirit. And may his grace be with all of you.
60973	2	1130	1	This letter is from Paul, a slave of God and an apostle of Jesus Christ. I have been sent to proclaim faith to those God has chosen and to teach them to know the truth that shows them how to live godly lives.
60974	2	1130	2	This truth gives them confidence that they have eternal life, which God—who does not lie—promised them before the world began.
60975	2	1130	3	And now at just the right time he has revealed this message, which we announce to everyone. It is by the command of God our Savior that I have been entrusted with this work for him.
60976	2	1130	4	I am writing to Titus, my true son in the faith that we share.\nMay God the Father and Christ Jesus our Savior give you grace and peace.
60977	2	1130	5	I left you on the island of Crete so you could complete our work there and appoint elders in each town as I instructed you.
60978	2	1130	6	An elder must live a blameless life. He must be faithful to his wife, and his children must be believers who don’t have a reputation for being wild or rebellious.
60979	2	1130	7	A church leader is a manager of God’s household, so he must live a blameless life. He must not be arrogant or quick-tempered; he must not be a heavy drinker, violent, or dishonest with money.
60980	2	1130	8	Rather, he must enjoy having guests in his home, and he must love what is good. He must live wisely and be just. He must live a devout and disciplined life.
60981	2	1130	9	He must have a strong belief in the trustworthy message he was taught; then he will be able to encourage others with wholesome teaching and show those who oppose it where they are wrong.
60982	2	1130	10	For there are many rebellious people who engage in useless talk and deceive others. This is especially true of those who insist on circumcision for salvation.
60983	2	1130	11	They must be silenced, because they are turning whole families away from the truth by their false teaching. And they do it only for money.
60984	2	1130	12	Even one of their own men, a prophet from Crete, has said about them, “The people of Crete are all liars, cruel animals, and lazy gluttons.”
60985	2	1130	13	This is true. So reprimand them sternly to make them strong in the faith.
60986	2	1130	14	They must stop listening to Jewish myths and the commands of people who have turned away from the truth.
60987	2	1130	15	Everything is pure to those whose hearts are pure. But nothing is pure to those who are corrupt and unbelieving, because their minds and consciences are corrupted.
60988	2	1130	16	Such people claim they know God, but they deny him by the way they live. They are detestable and disobedient, worthless for doing anything good.
60989	2	1131	1	As for you, Titus, promote the kind of living that reflects wholesome teaching.
60990	2	1131	2	Teach the older men to exercise self-control, to be worthy of respect, and to live wisely. They must have sound faith and be filled with love and patience.
60991	2	1131	3	Similarly, teach the older women to live in a way that honors God. They must not slander others or be heavy drinkers. Instead, they should teach others what is good.
60992	2	1131	4	These older women must train the younger women to love their husbands and their children,
60993	2	1131	5	to live wisely and be pure, to work in their homes, to do good, and to be submissive to their husbands. Then they will not bring shame on the word of God.
60994	2	1131	6	In the same way, encourage the young men to live wisely.
60995	2	1131	7	And you yourself must be an example to them by doing good works of every kind. Let everything you do reflect the integrity and seriousness of your teaching.
60996	2	1131	8	Teach the truth so that your teaching can’t be criticized. Then those who oppose us will be ashamed and have nothing bad to say about us.
60997	2	1131	9	Slaves must always obey their masters and do their best to please them. They must not talk back
60998	2	1131	10	or steal, but must show themselves to be entirely trustworthy and good. Then they will make the teaching about God our Savior attractive in every way.
60999	2	1131	11	For the grace of God has been revealed, bringing salvation to all people.
61000	2	1131	12	And we are instructed to turn from godless living and sinful pleasures. We should live in this evil world with wisdom, righteousness, and devotion to God,
61001	2	1131	13	while we look forward with hope to that wonderful day when the glory of our great God and Savior, Jesus Christ, will be revealed.
61002	2	1131	14	He gave his life to free us from every kind of sin, to cleanse us, and to make us his very own people, totally committed to doing good deeds.
61003	2	1131	15	You must teach these things and encourage the believers to do them. You have the authority to correct them when necessary, so don’t let anyone disregard what you say.
61004	2	1132	1	Remind the believers to submit to the government and its officers. They should be obedient, always ready to do what is good.
61005	2	1132	2	They must not slander anyone and must avoid quarreling. Instead, they should be gentle and show true humility to everyone.
61006	2	1132	3	Once we, too, were foolish and disobedient. We were misled and became slaves to many lusts and pleasures. Our lives were full of evil and envy, and we hated each other.
61007	2	1132	4	But—\nWhen God our Savior revealed his kindness and love,
61008	2	1132	5	he saved us, not because of the righteous things we had done, but because of his mercy. He washed away our sins, giving us a new birth and new life through the Holy Spirit.
61009	2	1132	6	He generously poured out the Spirit upon us through Jesus Christ our Savior.
61010	2	1132	7	Because of his grace he made us right in his sight and gave us confidence that we will inherit eternal life.
61011	2	1132	8	This is a trustworthy saying, and I want you to insist on these teachings so that all who trust in God will devote themselves to doing good. These teachings are good and beneficial for everyone.
61012	2	1132	9	Do not get involved in foolish discussions about spiritual pedigrees or in quarrels and fights about obedience to Jewish laws. These things are useless and a waste of time.
61013	2	1132	10	If people are causing divisions among you, give a first and second warning. After that, have nothing more to do with them.
61014	2	1132	11	For people like that have turned away from the truth, and their own sins condemn them.
61015	2	1132	12	I am planning to send either Artemas or Tychicus to you. As soon as one of them arrives, do your best to meet me at Nicopolis, for I have decided to stay there for the winter.
61016	2	1132	13	Do everything you can to help Zenas the lawyer and Apollos with their trip. See that they are given everything they need.
61017	2	1132	14	Our people must learn to do good by meeting the urgent needs of others; then they will not be unproductive.
61018	2	1132	15	Everybody here sends greetings. Please give my greetings to the believers—all who love us.\nMay God’s grace be with you all.
61019	2	1133	1	This letter is from Paul, a prisoner for preaching the Good News about Christ Jesus, and from our brother Timothy.\nI am writing to Philemon, our beloved co-worker,
61020	2	1133	2	and to our sister Apphia, and to our fellow soldier Archippus, and to the church that meets in your house.
61021	2	1133	3	May God our Father and the Lord Jesus Christ give you grace and peace.
61022	2	1133	4	I always thank my God when I pray for you, Philemon,
61023	2	1133	5	because I keep hearing about your faith in the Lord Jesus and your love for all of God’s people.
61024	2	1133	6	And I am praying that you will put into action the generosity that comes from your faith as you understand and experience all the good things we have in Christ.
61025	2	1133	7	Your love has given me much joy and comfort, my brother, for your kindness has often refreshed the hearts of God’s people.
61026	2	1133	8	That is why I am boldly asking a favor of you. I could demand it in the name of Christ because it is the right thing for you to do.
61027	2	1133	9	But because of our love, I prefer simply to ask you. Consider this as a request from me—Paul, an old man and now also a prisoner for the sake of Christ Jesus.
61028	2	1133	10	I appeal to you to show kindness to my child, Onesimus. I became his father in the faith while here in prison.
61029	2	1133	11	Onesimus hasn’t been of much use to you in the past, but now he is very useful to both of us.
61030	2	1133	12	I am sending him back to you, and with him comes my own heart.
61031	2	1133	13	I wanted to keep him here with me while I am in these chains for preaching the Good News, and he would have helped me on your behalf.
61032	2	1133	14	But I didn’t want to do anything without your consent. I wanted you to help because you were willing, not because you were forced.
61033	2	1133	15	It seems you lost Onesimus for a little while so that you could have him back forever.
61034	2	1133	16	He is no longer like a slave to you. He is more than a slave, for he is a beloved brother, especially to me. Now he will mean much more to you, both as a man and as a brother in the Lord.
61035	2	1133	17	So if you consider me your partner, welcome him as you would welcome me.
61036	2	1133	18	If he has wronged you in any way or owes you anything, charge it to me.
61037	2	1133	19	I, PAUL, WRITE THIS WITH MY OWN HAND: I WILL REPAY IT. AND I WON’T MENTION THAT YOU OWE ME YOUR VERY SOUL!
61038	2	1133	20	Yes, my brother, please do me this favor for the Lord’s sake. Give me this encouragement in Christ.
61039	2	1133	21	I am confident as I write this letter that you will do what I ask and even more!
61040	2	1133	22	One more thing—please prepare a guest room for me, for I am hoping that God will answer your prayers and let me return to you soon.
61041	2	1133	23	Epaphras, my fellow prisoner in Christ Jesus, sends you his greetings.
61042	2	1133	24	So do Mark, Aristarchus, Demas, and Luke, my co-workers.
61043	2	1133	25	May the grace of the Lord Jesus Christ be with your spirit.
61044	2	1134	1	Long ago God spoke many times and in many ways to our ancestors through the prophets.
61045	2	1134	2	And now in these final days, he has spoken to us through his Son. God promised everything to the Son as an inheritance, and through the Son he created the universe.
61046	2	1134	3	The Son radiates God’s own glory and expresses the very character of God, and he sustains everything by the mighty power of his command. When he had cleansed us from our sins, he sat down in the place of honor at the right hand of the majestic God in heaven.
